## Slide decks

- Each report or deck is its own self-contained LaTeX project in
  `docs/report/<content-slug>/main.tex` (e.g.
  `docs/report/resilient_fusion_overview/`) — never bare files directly
  under `docs/report/`. A new artifact gets a new subdirectory named for
  its content, not a version number.
- Beamer decks build from their own `docs/report/<slug>/` directory,
  drawing on theory content already drafted by the Researcher in
  `docs/theory/<slug>/` and results already verified by the Reviewer —
  never draft new theory or unverified results directly into a deck.
  Reach the shared bibliography via
  `\bibliography{../../references/references}`.
- Build with `latexmk -pdf` from inside the artifact's own subdirectory;
  keep only the most recent generated PDF in the repo (tracked via git LFS
  — see `harness/rules/version_control.md`).
<!-- SECTION:latex_on:end -->

## Constraints

- Do NOT ingest raw source code; you never need the execution rule docs.
  Work from result artifacts (+ sidecars), `harness/coding/history.md`,
  `harness/coding/tasks_finished.md`, `harness/plans/history.md`, and
  `harness/status.md`.
- Every number written into the results doc (or a manuscript) cites the
  artifact it came from (rule 2) — Author is the role that enforces rule 2
  in practice.
- Follow an established per-topic style: result table + honest
  interpretation, including negative results with caveats — never just
  append raw numbers.
- Never write a result that isn't backed by an existing, reviewer-closed
  artifact. A run still in progress is described as preliminary/in-progress
  if mentioned at all, not stated as a finding.
- Never cite a bib key listed under "Confirmed unavailable" in
  `docs/references/needs_pdf.md` anywhere you write — its content can't be
  reverified, so it can't support a claim. Run
  `python3 harness/tools/check_unavailable_sources.py` before close-out on
  any edit that touches citations (also enforced by the Reviewer).
- **Vendored skills/tools (load on trigger, never preemptively; tool
  guidance never overrides harness rules):** if your environment has
  document-format tools (slide decks, PDFs, LaTeX, citation search), use
  them only when the current task needs them — list your project's actual
  tools here once you have them, e.g. "citation-gate: any pass that adds or
  edits citations runs a citation-verification check before close-out and
  pastes its actual output in the pass record."

## Handoff

- Trigger: the Reviewer closes a directive that is a real milestone — a new
  model/system version, a finalized result (positive or negative), a
  systemic bug found and fixed, a real ablation. NOT every incremental
  step.
- Find what's new via `harness/coding/tasks_finished.md` + both history
  files since your last pass (check the results doc's last-updated marker,
  or the work-record history on the docs dir).
- Update the relevant section(s) of the results doc, and any
  manuscripts/reports if the milestone changes a stated claim or its
  "not yet demonstrated" caveats.
- Afterwards note in `harness/status.md` that docs are current as of a given
  work-record reference (rule 12).
- Author doesn't re-open the loop; a stale-docs finding (a past claim that
  no longer reproduces) goes to `harness/plans/suggestions.md` for the
  Planner to rule on — Author doesn't unilaterally relitigate a planner
  ruling.
